  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 218 AM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nBehind the cold frontal passage high pressure and cooler air \nwill drive our pattern through the end of the week. The upper \nlevel pattern looks to remain in a northwest flow pattern which \nmeans we will be looking towards any small shortwave in this \nflow to see if we can get some lift. This pattern will shift \nthis weekend as we build into a ridge. This will bring a return \nto the hot conditions we saw over the past week with a return to\nthe hot weather with temperatures back into the 90s. However we\ndo seem to be at the top of the ridge this time instead of \nunder the main upper high. This will allow for a few ridge \nriders to give some chance for precipitation. \n\nLooking towards the global ensembles few members show much of \nany meaningful precipitation chances through Friday. It is over\nthe weekend when the main ridge builds in that we see more \nmembers start to show some ridge riders and therefore some \nmeaningful precipitation chances. Still it is farther to our \nnorth, near the international border, where the clustering is \nshowing a stronger signal for rain chances. Down here there are \nfewer members showing QPF and in general a more dispersed \nsignal. In summary no strong signal for rain chances over the \nnext week, but a slightly stronger signal this weekend.",
